+# Futhark fork: the `rust-wgpu` backend
+
+A LOCAL fork of Futhark's `webgpu` branch (PR "Add WebGPU backend", head `14e9ccb`), never pushed anywhere. It adds
+one backend, `futhark rust-wgpu prog.fut -o prog`, which writes `prog.rs`: one Rust module holding the program's WGSL
+kernels, its kernel table and its host code over wgpu-rs, against the runtime crate `futhark-rust-rt` in fuller
+(`fuller/futhark-rust-rt`). The design is `fuller/docs/PLAN_futhark_rust_wgpu.md`.
+
+| change | where |
+|---|---|
+| the backend: ImpCode WebGPU (`ImpGen.WebGPU.compileProg`, the webgpu backend's input) to Rust | `src/Futhark/CodeGen/Backends/RustWGPU.hs` |
+| the command and the action | `src/Futhark/CLI/RustWGPU.hs`, `src/Futhark/CLI/Main.hs`, `src/Futhark/Actions.hs`, `futhark.cabal` |
+| `builtinKernels` exported (the copies and transpositions, described the same way for Rust) | `src/Futhark/CodeGen/Backends/CWebGPU.hs` |
+| `SetMem` in a GPU kernel resolved by renaming when it is outside every loop and conditional of the kernel (the webgpu backend's "Cannot handle SetMem" limitation; inside a loop or conditional it remains a compiler limitation, named) | `src/Futhark/CodeGen/ImpGen/WebGPU.hs` |
+
+Build: `./build_rust_wgpu.sh` (GHC 9.14.1 and cabal 3.18 from Homebrew; it sets the PATH and the ffi header the
+Homebrew GHC needs) installs `bin/futhark`. The SetMem change is in the shared WGSL kernel generator, so it also
+changes what this fork's `webgpu` backend emits; fuller's shim path uses the pinned upstream CI binary, not this fork.
